{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrierBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrierBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.hbarGen_six_bar_even_dressing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.hbarGen_six_bar_even_dressing","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCarrierBarParity.lean#L117-L125","doc":"**The bar-even repair of the `(6,1)` pattern is `q³`, not `q`.**\n\nThe `ℏ_q⁶` prefactor is bar-even only when dressed by `q³`, and `ℏ_q⁶·q³ = w³`.\nSo the nearest bar-even relative of the R9 rung lives in the `w`-tower at\n`j = 3`. (The probe then shows that tower admits no order with a small-height\ncoefficient: `t/w³ = 0.16211 < 1/5` and `t/w⁴ = 14.877 > 5`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.hbarGen_monomial_six_one_not_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.hbarGen_monomial_six_one_not_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCarrierBarParity.lean#L108-L115","doc":"**Selection rule, negative half (witness form).** A monomial whose `q`-power\nis *not* half its `ℏ_q`-power is not bar-even. Exhibited on the exponent pattern\n`(k, m) = (6, 1)` — exactly the shape of `MmuR9V9Closure.delta_R9` — at `q = 2`:\n`ℏ_2⁶·2 = 1/32` while `ℏ_{1/2}⁶·(1/2) = 1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.hbarGen_monomial_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.hbarGen_monomial_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCarrierBarParity.lean#L98-L106","doc":"**Selection rule, corollary.** Consequently every such monomial is bar-even:\n\n`ℏ_{q⁻¹}^{2j} · (q⁻¹)^j = ℏ_q^{2j} · q^j`.\n\nSo the bar-even part of the `ℏ_q`-monomial family is exactly the `w`-tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.hbarGen_pow_two_mul_eq_wGen_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.hbarGen_pow_two_mul_eq_wGen_pow","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCarrierBarParity.lean#L91-L96","doc":"**Selection rule, positive half.** The monomial `ℏ_q^{2j} · q^{j}` — the only\n`(k, m)` pattern with `k = 2m` — *is* the `j`-th power of `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.wGen_eq_q_mul_hbarGen_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.wGen_eq_q_mul_hbarGen_sq","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCarrierBarParity.lean#L84-L89","doc":"`w` is the `q`-dressed square of the substrate: `w_q = q · ℏ_q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.wGen_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.wGen_bar","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCarrierBarParity.lean#L78-L82","doc":"`w` is bar-invariant: `w_{q⁻¹} = w_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.hbarGen_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.hbarGen_bar","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCarrierBarParity.lean#L66-L76","doc":"**The bar involution does not fix `ℏ_q`.** Applying `q ↦ q⁻¹` multiplies it\nby `−q`:\n\n  `ℏ_{q⁻¹} = −q · ℏ_q`.\n\nThis single identity drives the whole selection rule below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.wGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.wGen","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCarrierBarParity.lean#L63-L64","doc":"`w := [2]_q − 2 = q + q⁻¹ − 2`, over a generic field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.hbarGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrier.hbarGen","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCarrierBarParity.lean#L59-L61","doc":"Substrate `ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹`, over a generic field. Agrees with the production\n`QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ` on `ℝ` (see `MuPCarrierOrderWindow.hbarGen_eq_hbarQ`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}